{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>For</b> — סורר means one who turns aside from the path that He commanded not to walk in. And behold, he compared Israel to a stubborn cow, with which a man cannot plow. And the meaning of 'now HaShem will shepherd them like a sheep in a wide pasture' [is] — were you not stubborn? Or the meaning is: now HaShem will pasture them like a sheep alone in a wide place, and he [who says this] is mistaken."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:07.245863504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}